From 80de9f2871a4a26482fade288c16aee94453583a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:20:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: minimum width on Auto, puncturing inputs,
 interference mitigation, Stateful SLAAC, SDN DNS route

- Minimum width on Auto (rc/reaper_bwfloor.c, new): per-radio wlN_bwfloor
  appends the radio's 20/40 MHz chanspecs to wlN_acs_excl_chans at the end of
  set_acs_ifnames(), records them under /jffs/reaper_bwfloor/, strips exactly
  those first; watcher lifts after 120 s below floor or 180 s dark outside CAC
  (30 min, doubling, cap 4 h). A re-arm while the radio is already wide marks
  it picker-pending instead of restarting acsd2. Page lock rule on Auto bw.
- Dynamic puncturing (rpunctd): scan neighbour inventory + PHY figures as
  priors; per-tick chanim PHY trigger with a noise baseline; station-table
  client evidence (bs_data -noreset windows) with tie-break and a 120 s
  better/worse proof; a scan that loses a client stops scans on that radio;
  the Active source never scans above 30 % own airtime (PC_SCAN_OWN_MAX).
- Interference mitigation (wlN_rmit, applied by reaper_punct mit_pass):
  Driver default writes nothing; "hwaci" sets the driver mask | 16; records
  the base and undoes only its own write; state /tmp/reaper_wlmit.state,
  wlN_rmit_st for the page; rwatch re-runs the applier while set; rpunctd
  resets its noise baseline and impairment state on a change.
- IPv6: Stateful with a /64 adds slaac to the dnsmasq dhcp-range (and the
  constructor form) so SLAAC-only hosts get an address (GT-BE98 field).
- wan.c: dns_in_sdn_subnet() skips the WAN /32 host route for a DNS server
  inside a saved SDN subnet (get_mtsubnet); a resolver on a VLAN was routed
  out the WAN.
- AiMesh topology: node cards on a non-routing box overlay reaper_dev.cgi's
  via field (GT-BE19000 field).
- reaper_diag v1.3.25: section 6 IPv6 autoconf/range/leases/firewall
  findings; section 7 min width and interference lines.
- Tokens: RWFP additions incl. RWFP_124-129; 25 packs in lockstep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
